---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// The third presence treatment, and the one that is hardest to argue
// against on looks. It keeps the text at full strength, unlike the dim,
// so it passes contrast on its own terms. It loses for a different
// reason: the row already changes its background on hover, so on a
// pointer the two states are nearly the same picture, and a signal that
// says "somebody is here" cannot also be the signal that says "your
// mouse is here".
//
// Worth saying out loud after the dim: this one is not rejected on a
// measurement. It is rejected because the background was already spoken
// for, which is the kind of collision you only find by building the
// thing into a row that already has states.
//
// Drive it: hover a row that nobody is in, then look at the row somebody
// is in. That is the whole argument.
---

<Slide subtitle="Multiplayer → Highlight the row" badge="Rejected">
	<iframe
		src="/decks/2026-checklist-component/prototypes/edit-presence-bench?embed=1&scale=1.6&solo=1&mark=floathi&fit=center"
		title="The row highlight, rejected for colliding with hover"
		class="live-embed m-0! block h-[800px] w-[1704px] max-h-none! max-w-none! border-0"
	></iframe>
</Slide>
